How to reproduce on real removable media instead of a file
blkid_verify() does not require a block device — it open()s the path and lseek/reads it, so a regular file is a faithful stand-in. To exercise the genuine vold path:

dd if=ntfs_poc.bin of=/dev/<sdcard-block-device>
# reinsert the card; vold runs /system/bin/blkid on it before any fsck or mount
I did not perform this step, because it needs a sanitizer-instrumented /system/bin/blkid on a userdebug build; the file-backed reproduction above exercises identical code with identical arguments.

