One honest note on coverage
ntfs_poc.bin (site A) produces the UBSan shift report under HWASan but NOT a tag-mismatch, where ASan does report a heap-buffer-overflow. HWASan's tag granule is 16 bytes, so a 4-byte read just past a small allocation can land inside the same granule and go unseen. The two sanitizers are complementary here; ASan is the one that catches site A.

